// Local, free/personal-team real-device testing — see
// .claude/notes/18-ios-personal-team-signing.md. Same idea as Config/
// Debug.xcconfig (ENABLE_PUSH=NO, no aps-environment), but goes further:
// its entitlements file also omits com.apple.developer.associated-domains
// (added to the ordinary Debug/Release entitlements in the 2026-10-01 UX
// foundation pass for Universal Links), so this configuration can never
// fail to sign over ANY capability this project currently declares that
// isn't confirmed to work on a free/personal team.
//
// Development builds have to NAME the team: a command-line `xcodebuild` does
// not fall back to whichever Apple Account Xcode happens to have selected (it
// fails with "No Account for Team"). The team is NOT written here — it lives in
// the gitignored Config/PersonalTeam.xcconfig beside this file, included
// optionally below, so no developer's personal team ID is committed. Create it
// once per Mac (Xcode > Settings > Accounts shows the ID):
//
//   echo "DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = XXXXXXXXXX" > Config/PersonalTeam.xcconfig
//
// Without that file nothing is baked in: builds started from Xcode's Run button
// still sign with the account selected there, and Tools/run-on-device.sh prints
// this same hint if signing fails. A command-line DEVELOPMENT_TEAM still wins
// over the included file. Config/Team.xcconfig — the PAID team Debug/Release
// inherit — is deliberately not included here and stays untouched (still empty
// until a paid account exists, see .claude/notes/07-notifications.md).
ENABLE_PUSH = NO
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = BanbeApp/BanbeApp.PersonalTeam.entitlements
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
// Optional, untracked: the personal team this Mac signs device builds with.
#include? "PersonalTeam.xcconfig"
SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) PERSONAL_TEAM_BUILD
